                <pb facs="0290" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg170"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee authorizes Mr. Rockhill to sound other legations in regard to the
                    protection of trade-marks in China, and, if they be duly authorized by their
                    governments, to effect arrangements by an exchange of notes on the basis of the
                    British precedent.)</p>
            </div>
